<title>UK: HORSE RACING-KING GEORGE VI CHASE RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-KING GEORGE VI CHASE RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the King George VI Chase</p>
<p>for five-year-olds and upwards, run over three miles (4.8 kms)</p>
<p>at Kempton on Thursday:</p>
<p>1. One Man 13-8 on favourite (ridden by Richard Dunwoody) 2.</p>
<p>Rough Quest 4-1 (Mick Fitzgerald) 3. Barton Bank 10-1 (Adrian</p>
<p>Maguire)</p>
<p>Five ran</p>
<p>Distances: 12 lengths, nine</p>
<p>Winner owned by John Hales and trained in England by Gordon</p>
<p>Richards.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 66,325 pounds ($111,000)</p>
</text>
